        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cairo Junction, Cairo, Illinois\n- Roads: U.S. Route 51, Illinois Route 3, Illinois Route 37, Interstate 39\n- Topics: Highway location, highway route, highway replacement\n\nFacts:\n- U.S. Route 51 is a south-north United States highway that runs 1,286 miles from the western suburbs of New Orleans, Louisiana, to within 100 feet of the Wisconsin–Michigan border.\n- In the early 1980s, U.S. Route 51 was one of the busiest two-lane highways in the United States.\n- Interstate 39 was designed to replace U.S. Route 51.\n- Cairo Junction, Illinois, is located at the junction of U.S. Route 51, Illinois Route 3, and Illinois Route 37 north of Cairo.",
